<h3>Toll Handling and State Regulations</h3>
<p>The Noida to Kolkata corridor is a mix of National Highways and State Highways, each with different toll structures. While many National Highways utilize Fastag-enabled automatic toll gates, several state-managed stretches may still require cash or manual processing. This variability creates friction points during peak hours.</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Fastag Compliance:</strong> All vehicles must have active Fastag accounts with sufficient balance to ensure non-stop passage through automatic gates.</li>
    <li><strong>State-Specific Entry Fees:</strong> Some states levy additional entry charges for commercial vehicles crossing their borders, regardless of the destination.</li>
    <li><strong>Weight Restrictions:</strong> Oversized or overweight loads are strictly regulated at weighbridges. Non-compliance here is a major cause of route deviation and delay.</li>
    <li><strong>Time-Based Restrictions:</strong> Certain high-density urban areas in Kolkata impose time windows for commercial vehicle entry, requiring precise scheduling of the final leg of the journey.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Real-Time Logistics Advisories</h3>
<p>Road conditions on the Noida to Kolkata route are dynamic. Weather events, road construction, and traffic congestion can alter transit times significantly. Real-time monitoring is essential for maintaining accurate delivery estimates.</p>
